  "label": "Comparative Juxtaposition Scene",
  "description": "The scene presents a visual and textual contrast between two identical images of a woman in a hijab, each accompanied by a different text overlay. The top panel questions how a woman can receive free home and benefits, while the bottom panel states that a man died on the streets after serving the country. The scene uses the identical visual of the woman to imply a moral or ethical comparison, suggesting she is undeserving of aid while implying the man is more deserving. The spatial arrangement places the woman centrally in both panels, with text positioned to the right, creating a direct visual and rhetorical contrast.",
